{"id": "EUVD-2026-99261", "enisaUuid": "45d81c62-f5fd-30ae-a96a-f6756a9cc6ec", "description": "Kubeflow Model Registry through 0.3.17 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows namespace users to steal the controller ServiceAccount token via the modelregistry.kubeflow.org/url annotation. Attackers can create an InferenceService pointing the annotation at their server, capture the bearer token, and modify other tenants' InferenceServices cluster-wide.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:50:07", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/kubeflow-hub-controller-token-url-forwarding", "https://github.com/kubeflow/hub/blob/v0.3.17/pkg/inferenceservice-controller/controller.go#L268-L292", "https://github.com/kubeflow/hub/blob/v0.3.17/pkg/openapi/client.go#L420-L423", "https://github.com/kubeflow/hub/blob/v0.3.17/cmd/controller/main.go#L224-L228", "https://github.com/kubeflow/hub", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/kubeflow-model-registry-through-0.3.17-ssrf-via-inferenceservice-controller-url-annotation"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q9m2-3393-574q", "CVE-2026-110220"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3197a74b-804d-3d71-94bd-c64cdc89b406", "product": {"name": "Model Registry", "vendor": {"name": "kubeflow"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.3.17"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b5834461-b415-3101-966d-4c45e900702f", "vendor": {"name": "kubeflow"}}], "isExploited": false}